arguments are basically variables that you put in front of your script name and it is used to make your script interactive-less. Eg in the script if you have echo "Script Name: $0" in the first line, and echo "First Argument: $1" in the second, and echo "Second Argument: $2" in the third line, and you run this script with ./arg.sh apple banana, you will have the arg.sh in the script name, apple in the first argument and banana in the second

To get the total number of arguments, use echo "no of args: $#", and to get all the arguments used in one line, echo "all arguments: $*"